 ## Unreleased
 
+- **Chat can show only AI text replies** (V-1271). The “AI replies only” toggle above the chat hides user/agent deliveries, tools/results, thinking and status rows while preserving ordinary assistant text and live streams. Existing history, older pages and new events share the timeline's text classification. Switching back restores retained DOM nodes without a reload; the existing localStorage preference pattern remembers the choice, with the full journal as the default. No server/API/history-store changes.
 - **Local retained close when a Hub thread is absent** (V-1268). On a bounded `t3_thread_read` that returns the structured `thread_not_found` for the exact owned workspace thread, the existing session-removal path archives the local session card while retaining its logs, accounting, worktree, Hub state, privacy latch, manifest, provenance and unresolved non-dispatchable delivery records. It performs no remote mutation or workspace cleanup. Pending sync, active jobs, ambiguous or changed generation, transient read errors, pending Hub requests and dispatchable queued message/initial deliveries still block. Ordinary Hub archival and its privacy guards are unchanged; no new API or archive store is introduced.
 - **Bounded Argon specialist through the existing paid Hub pool** (V-1257; owner decisions 2026-11-03 14:52 and 15:31). Only the default-pipeline specialist with a bound task/project scope may use `hub-gemini-4-argon`, mapped to `antigravity/gemini-4-argon`, for design, document synthesis/comparison and financial/legal reasoning on public or synthetic text. General terminal/repository coding stays on Hub Sol; native Codex orchestration is unchanged. Video, media ingestion, large context, long-decode and Google-app integration remain unverified in Hub; maker-reported API capabilities are not platform guarantees. Canonical admission rechecks existing identity at creation, model changes, deliveries, backend submission and recovery; the same specialist instructions reach initial and resumed Hub turns. Antigravity retains provider-capacity admission and the shared turn limit; absent telemetry is visible as unknown and context/modality/prices are not invented. Phase A stages the role with known Sol; the separate Phase B patch selects Gemini only after root verifies the live registry through normal idle activation. No manual restart, worker/queue migration, API/Carbon/overage/auxiliary-image fallback or early inference. Offline checks do not substitute for the post-activation safe file-writing smoke.
 - **Research closure requires an explanation delivered to the owner** (V-1256; owner decision 2026-11-03). The existing user-answer-format owns the substantive verdict, coverage, interpretable numbers, mechanisms, examples, counter-evidence, failed/skipped checks, limits and practical implications. Default replies are short and dense: verdict, decision-relevant numbers and practical implication/next action; expand only on request or to explain a material risk. Shared orchestration and lifecycle instructions check evidence acceptance and actual owner delivery before research closure; sub-orchestrators pass complete findings and outstanding delivery obligations through their parent. DONE, an artifact path, status text and acknowledgement suppression cannot replace or hide the result. Approval boundaries, artifact reading, model-review freeze, worker routing and fresh-instance policy remain unchanged. Prompt-only correction; no task-state/runtime contract, new approval phase, provider call, deployment or adherence measurement.
